# For more info on HTTP files go to https://aka.ms/vs/httpfile
#
# Every MS4 endpoint requires a bearer token from nur-tricenter-identity (scope per endpoint, see
# Nur.Tricenter.Access DeliveryCalendarPermission). Two ways to run this file:
#
#  - Nur-Tricenter platform (nur-tricenter-local start-stack): use the gateway as host, run
#    request "0. Login" first — its token is reused by every other request.
#  - Standalone (Aspire): there is no identity; paste a token signed with the AppHost's dev key
#    ("Parameters:jwt-secret") into @token, or test through Scalar.
#
# Standalone (Aspire):
# @Api_HostAddress = https://localhost:7206
# Platform (gateway, MS4 published as /api/delivery-calendar):
@Gateway = http://localhost:15005
@Api_HostAddress = {{Gateway}}/api/delivery-calendar
@token = {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}
@contractId = 11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111
@patientId = 22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222222
@planId = 33333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333333
@calendarId = 1
@dayId = 1

### 0. Login as the platform administrator (holds every deliveryCalendar.* scope)
# @name login
POST {{Gateway}}/api/identity-service/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userName": "admin",
  "password": "admin"
}

### 1. Create schedule (MS3) — idempotent by contractId
POST {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/v1/schedule
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "contractId": "{{contractId}}",
  "patientId": "{{patientId}}",
  "planId": "{{planId}}",
  "duration": 15,
  "startDate": "2026-08-01"
}

### 2. Get calendar
GET {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/v1/calendars/{{calendarId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 3. Set delivery address (Frontend)
POST {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/v1/calendars/{{calendarId}}/addresses
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "dayId": {{dayId}},
  "street": "Main St 123",
  "city": "Springfield",
  "latitude": 10.5,
  "longitude": -20.25,
  "references": "Gate 2",
  "notes": "Ring twice"
}

### 4. Reschedule delivery date (Frontend) — rejected with 409 if <48h away
PUT {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/v1/calendars/{{calendarId}}/dates
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "dayId": {{dayId}},
  "newDate": "2026-08-20"
}

### 5. Cancel delivery day (Frontend) — rejected with 409 if <48h away
POST {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/v1/calendars/{{calendarId}}/cancel-day
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "dayId": {{dayId}}
}

### 6. Internal/ops — manually trigger daily catalog resolution job (not part of CLAUDE.md §0 contract)
POST {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/v1/calendars/resolve-daily-catalog?date=2026-08-01
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 7. Get active-tomorrow production order (MS3)
GET {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/v1/calendars/active-tomorrow?date=2026-08-01
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 8. Apply delivery result (MS5) — idempotent when called twice with the same result
PATCH {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/v1/calendars/days/{{dayId}}/delivery-result
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "result": "Delivered",
  "photoUrl": "https://example.com/evidence.jpg",
  "signatureUrl": null
}

### 9. Lookup — calendar of a contract (404 until MS3 creates it)
GET {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/v1/calendars/by-contract/{{contractId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 10. Lookup — calendars of a patient (newest first)
GET {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/v1/calendars/by-patient/{{patientId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 11. Lookup — MS5 delivery/route linked to a day (null fields until MS5 routes it)
GET {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/v1/calendars/days/{{dayId}}/delivery-link
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
